From: Ahrion Gallegos <ahrionmgallegos@gmail.com>
Subject: quectel-5g-tools: drop the ModemManager dependency + watchdog

This fork's modem stack is QModem + the Quectel vendor pcie_mhi
driver; ModemManager is not in the image at all. quectel-5g-tools'
Makefile hard-depends on +modemmanager, which silently pulls MM (and
its dbus/glib2/libmbim tail) back into every build — defeating the
stack swap.

The only piece of quectel-5g-tools that actually needs MM is
5g-watchdog (it polls `mmcli -J` and drives recovery through
netifd's proto=modemmanager). Everything else — 5g-info, 5g-monitor,
5g-lock, 5g-led-bars, quectel-at, modem-debug, the Prometheus
collectors — talks raw AT to /dev/ttyUSB2 and works fine without MM.

So: drop +modemmanager from DEPENDS and stop installing the
5g-watchdog binary + init script (it would just crash-loop without
mmcli). Session recovery is quectel-CM's job under QModem. The
/etc/modemmanager/ignore-tty file still gets installed; it's inert
without MM and not worth a bigger diff.

Applied by prepare.sh against the .build-deps/ checkout (which is
reset to the pinned ref on every run, so this re-applies each time).
If it stops applying, vjt's quectel-5g-tools master has drifted —
refresh the hunks.

--- a/.build-deps/quectel-5g-tools/openwrt/quectel-5g-tools/Makefile
+++ b/.build-deps/quectel-5g-tools/openwrt/quectel-5g-tools/Makefile
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ define Package/quectel-5g-tools
   SECTION:=net
   CATEGORY:=Network
   TITLE:=Quectel 5G Modem Tools
-  DEPENDS:=+lua +luaposix +libuci-lua +luci-lib-jsonc +modemmanager +curl
+  DEPENDS:=+lua +luaposix +libuci-lua +luci-lib-jsonc +curl
   URL:=https://github.com/vjt/quectel-5g-tools
 endef

@@ -83,7 +83,6 @@ define Package/quectel-5g-tools/install
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/5g-info $(1)/usr/bin/
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/5g-monitor $(1)/usr/bin/
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/5g-led-bars $(1)/usr/bin/
-	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/5g-watchdog $(1)/usr/bin/
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/at $(1)/usr/bin/quectel-at
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/5g-lock $(1)/usr/bin/
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/bin/modem-debug $(1)/usr/bin/
@@ -91,7 +90,6 @@ define Package/quectel-5g-tools/install
 	# Install procd init scripts
 	$(INSTALL_DIR) $(1)/etc/init.d
 	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/etc/init.d/5g-led-bars $(1)/etc/init.d/
-	$(INSTALL_BIN) $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/etc/init.d/5g-watchdog $(1)/etc/init.d/

 	# Tell ModemManager to skip the Quectel USB AT/DIAG/NMEA/AT2 ports
 	# (/dev/ttyUSB0..3). The patched /etc/hotplug.d/tty/25-modemmanager-tty
